ADD
- I-12 — D2 "conflicting flags fail preflight" never enumerates conflict pairs (`--mode auto --use-print`, `--mode non-interactive --use-interactive`, `--mode interactive --use-print`); implementers will diverge.
- I-13 — `--no-escalate` / `SB_AGENT_NO_ESCALATE=1` does not suppress §4.1 prior-wave force-interactive rule, so "no escalate" still pins interactive forever on a reused `task-id` even when classifier should pick NI.
- I-14 — `events.jsonl` and `escalation.md` schemas (required fields, log-tail length, retry-prompt shape) not enumerated; only example event names listed.
- I-15 — §5.1 step 3 "optional read-only `monitor.sh` on the log file" is a second wrapper process, contradicting D7 NI "no extra bash wrapper beyond invoke.sh → delegate.sh → exec."
- I-16 — Snapshot redaction in §5.2, but `events.jsonl` stream (assistant text, tool_use payloads) is unredacted — credential-leak path secret-scan does not cover.
- I-17 — §6.2 `--control-dir` on NI behavior unspecified (I-11 flags it; behavior = `mode-conflict` vs silent-ignore is a separate risk vs D6 fail-closed).
